Probably not often nowadays. But when I started playing Hack about 20
years ago, I had a computer that didn't use any operating system Hack was
ported to. So I played remote. 
And those days it meant playing through a modem connection. And the modems
of those days didn't yet have error correction. Sometimes there was enough
garbage caused by the bad connection that the screen actually needed to be
redrawn every now and then to make any sense.

^r is probably these days one of the least used commands, if not THE least
used one. 
Some other rarely used commands could be #quit (well, SOME people use it
for character rerolling..) ! ^Z V X F $ #monster #turn #version #wipe.

